ic.com/health/2026/11/measles-elimination-status-endemic-kennedy/689450/?utm_source=feed" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link></entry><entry><id>tag:theatlantic.com,2026:50-689295</id><author><name>Hana Kiros</name><uri>http://www.theatlantic.com/author/hana-kiros/?utm_source=feed</uri></author><media:content url="https://cdn.theatlantic.com/thumbor/KPG8sUD9cC_Ug4Oqu5nNC8rqrD8=/media/img/mt/2026/11/2026_10_20_The_U.S._Is_Sitting_Out_a_Famine_for_the_First_Time_in_Decades_Hana_Kiros/original.jpg"><media:credit>Brian Otieno / The New York Times / Redux</media:credit></media:content><title type="html">An ‘America First’ Approach to Famine</title><published>2026-11-08T08:00:00-05:00</published><updated>2026-11-08T08:46:53-05:00</updated><summary type="html">Somalia is experiencing a hunger emergency. For the first time in decades, the U.S. isn’t doing anything to stop it.</summary><link href="https://www.theatlantic.com/health/2026/11/famine-somalia-trump-aid/689295/?utm_source=feed" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link></entry></feed>